This research introduces the MusicTM-Dataset, a comprehensive collection of music notation, text, and audio that enables cross-modal learning. The dataset comprises three parts: visual, with lyrics and staff lines represented as text, and audio, with audio signals. The dataset is designed to facilitate the development of unified representations through a joint learning approach across these three modalities. The proposed method was tested on three benchmark tasks and outperformed a baseline method, demonstrating the effectiveness of this approach. The dataset and corresponding code can be accessed at the provided link. 

